From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:18:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: allow peer mappings that end at the last page of a
 BAR

nv_dma_map_peer() compared the exclusive end of the request with
res->end, which is the last valid address of the BAR. A range ending at
the top of the BAR was therefore rejected, so a dma-buf, nv-p2p or
GPU-to-GPU mapping that included the last page failed with
NV_ERR_INVALID_REQUEST. Compare the last byte instead, as IS_FB_OFFSET()
does, and reject a request that wraps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c
index bf7862d2..9368a12a 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c
@@ -809,7 +809,10 @@ NV_STATUS NV_API_CALL nv_dma_map_peer
         return NV_ERR_INVALID_REQUEST;
     }
 
-    if ((*va < res->start) || ((*va + (page_count * PAGE_SIZE)) > res->end))
+    /* res->end is the last valid address of the BAR, not one past it. */
+    if ((*va < res->start) ||
+        ((*va + (page_count * PAGE_SIZE) - 1) < *va) ||
+        ((*va + (page_count * PAGE_SIZE) - 1) > res->end))
     {
         NV_DMA_DEV_PRINTF(NV_DBG_ERRORS, peer_dma_dev,
                 "Mapping requested (start = 0x%llx, page_count = 0x%llx)"
